# Chapter 16 requests. Start the app first: dotnet run --urls http://127.0.0.1:42148
# The app's /catalog route stands in for the downstream catalog, so the order route calls the same host.
# Each "Expect" line is the status you should see. Watch the console for the JSON log line, the
# trace and the orders.created metric after each order.

@host = http://127.0.0.1:42148

###
# Liveness only. Expect 200 "Healthy"
GET {{host}}/health/live

###
# Readiness includes the catalog check. Expect 200 "Healthy"
GET {{host}}/health/ready

###
# Create an order. Expect 201 and the same X-Correlation-ID response header
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-ID: order-lab-1

{ "region": "east" }

###
# An unsafe correlation ID is replaced with the trace ID. Expect 201 and a different X-Correlation-ID
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-ID: bad id with spaces

{ "region": "west" }

###
# Regions other than east and west are rejected. Expect 400
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "region": "north" }

###
# The stand-in catalog can fail on request. Expect 503
GET {{host}}/catalog?status=503
